@lurch The Java viewer is supported in VNC 5.3.x, although we're working on a replacement technology since fewer and fewer browsers support the necessary Java plugin any more.

However, I don't think this is how @windy54 is trying to connect - it looks like noVNC is being used to connect to a virtual-mode VNC server, and then provide a web-based proxy to a VNC session. This mechanism _should_ work, but is not something we routinely test against. It may require tweaks to the commands needed to launch vncserver, as the command-line options for the RealVNC version have evolved from the tightvnc and other versions based on the original RealVNC open-source implementation.

I can't see anything in the [teacher's guide](https://www.raspberrypi.org/learning/teachers-guide/remote/) about accessing a VNC Server from the web - is this documented elsewhere?

@LornaLynch ah, I'm afraid that while you did make a correction to the language, you didn't merge the PR first. I.e. your correction wound up as [a second commit](https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/pull/448/commits/467fee436fea7f3b07918f753f04aa800ef16322) within the PR's branch (GitHub recently added the ability for contributors to add their own commits to others' PRs). You then added [another language correction commit](https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/commit/aaeb4074f1f9179df0da0cbe7de5570444dd7acc) but on the master branch. Because this hit the same line as this PR, but occurred _after_ this PR on the master branch, it conflicted.

If all this is hard to visualize, have a look at the [network graph](https://github.com/raspberrypi/documentation/network) for the project. You should be able to find Spencer's original commit fairly easily (look along from the spencer1573 line). Then note that your initial correction commit is after his _on the same branch_; that branch wasn't merged to master prior to that commit being made. Then have a look at the next chronological commit on master which is your second correction commit; this is the one that hits the same line as Spencer's initial PR. Because it's on the master branch _after_ Spencer's commit, it's a conflict which would require Spencer to rebase his commit on master to fix (or just close this and open a new PR which starts after the conflicting commit, which is what was ultimately done).

Hope that clarifies things!

